WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.440
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.900
It's the merger.
是合并那一集。

9
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.360
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

10
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.640
We're merging.
我们要合并了。

11
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.960
Where are we merging to?
我们要合并到哪里去？

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:37.120
We are merging two worlds today, Angela, the Stanford and the Scranton branches.
安吉拉，今天我们要合并两个世界，斯坦福分部和斯克兰顿分部。

13
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.100
Not all of the Stanford branch, but some will be merging with Scranton.
不是整个斯坦福分部，但有一部分人要和斯克兰顿合并。

14
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.020
I also feel like we're merging as friends because I'm looking at you.
而且我觉得我们作为朋友也在“合并”，因为我正看着你。

15
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.040
I think we have almost the same outfit on today.
我觉得我们今天穿得几乎一模一样。

16
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:55.380
You know, I mean, seriously, like they always say like pet owners start to look like their pets.
你知道，我是说，真的，就像人们常说的，宠物主人会变得越来越像他们的宠物。

17
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.700
Best friends start to look like each other and like husbands and wives and partners.
最好的朋友会变得越来越像对方，就像夫妻和伴侣一样。

18
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.500
Like I feel like we're starting to look like each other.
我觉得我们也开始变得越来越像对方了。

19
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.960
We might be.
可能吧。

20
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.060
Also, neither one of us has had a haircut or a hair color in a very long time.
而且，我们俩都已经很久没剪头发或染头发了。

21
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.020
I did my own hair color, lady.
我自己染的头发，女士。

22
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.080
I did too.
我也是。

23
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.680
Well, actually, Lee did mine with my hair colorist on FaceTime.
其实，是李通过FaceTime指导我的染发师帮我染的。

24
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.900
I did mine.
我自己弄的。

25
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.520
But no, I haven't had a haircut.
但确实，我没剪过头发。

26
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.640
And I kind of have given up on makeup.
而且我基本上已经放弃化妆了。

27
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:23.780
Just lipstick.
只涂口红。

28
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.320
Do you notice I only wear lipstick?
你注意到我只涂口红了吗？

29
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.340
Yeah, you show up to these Zooms in lipstick.
注意到了，你每次参加Zoom会议都涂着口红。

30
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:34.700
I was walking out to my That's What She Said to start the Zoom and I put on a little lipstick and the kids were like, why are you putting on lipstick?
我刚才正要走出去录“这就是她说的”，准备开始Zoom会议，我涂了点口红，孩子们就问我，为什么要涂口红？

31
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.660
And I was like, because I'm, yeah, because.
我就说，因为我……对，因为我要开会。

32
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.280
Yes, I will be on a Zoom.
是的，我要参加Zoom会议。

33
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.760
I'm going to be on a Zoom.
我要去开Zoom会议了。

34
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.440
All right.
好吧。

35
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:53.040
Well, this is season three, episode eight, written by Brent Forrester and directed by Ken Whittingham.
这一集是第三季第八集，由布伦特·福雷斯特编剧，肯·惠廷汉执导。

36
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.100
Do you want a summary?
你需要剧情梗概吗？

37
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.100
I do want a summary.
我确实需要。

38
00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:56.840
All right.
好的。

39
00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.180
Good.
太好了。

40
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:05.000
The Stanford branch merges with the Scranton branch, which means Jim will be returning to his old stomping ground.
斯坦福分部与斯克兰顿分部合并，这意味着吉姆将回到他熟悉的老地方。

41
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:05.620
Oh.
哦。

42
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:06.420
Oh.
哦。

43
00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:07.600
Woo-hoo-hoo.
呜呼呼。

44
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.360
Bam is so excited.
巴姆太兴奋了。

45
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:17.280
Michael does his best to welcome the Stanford transplants, but he goes a bit too far, causing one employee to quit.
迈克尔尽其所能欢迎来自斯坦福的同事，但他做得有点过火，导致一名员工辞职。

46
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:25.840
But Michael tries to save face by then firing him, leaving Dunder Mifflin with having to pay a sizable severance.
但迈克尔为了挽回面子，转而解雇了他，导致邓德·米夫林公司不得不支付一笔可观的遣散费。

47
00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.980
Jan's not happy.
简很不高兴。

48
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.060
Jan is not happy.
简非常不高兴。

49
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:38.040
Meanwhile, Pam senses something is going on with Jim and Karen and Dwight clashes with Andy.
与此同时，帕姆察觉到吉姆和凯伦之间有些不对劲，而德怀特则与安迪发生了冲突。

50
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.360
Good summary, lady.
总结得好，女士。

51
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.200
Thanks.
谢谢。

52
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.560
You know what I started realizing?
你知道我开始意识到什么了吗？

53
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.460
What?
什么？

54
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.540
You know how I have that Bible from The Office?
你知道我有那本《办公室》圣经吗？

55
00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.560
The Office Bible?
《办公室》圣经？

56
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.080
Yeah.
对。

57
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:48.520
Yeah.
没错。

58
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.380
Every show has a summary.
每一集都有剧情梗概。

59
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.980
Every episode has a summary in The Office Bible.
《办公室》圣经里每一集都有梗概。

60
00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.600
So I've been able to now refer to The Office Bible summary.
所以我现在可以参考《办公室》圣经里的梗概了。

61
00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.920
I tweak it a little.
我会稍微调整一下。

62
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.560
I put a little zhuzh on it.
加点润色。

63
00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:06.420
But yeah, I used to just sit down at a blank page and think, how do I summarize this episode?
以前我总是对着空白页面发愁，心想该怎么总结这一集呢？

64
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:12.160
And a team of writers have done it for me, and it was just sitting on my desk.
现在编剧团队已经帮我写好了，而且就放在我的桌子上。

65
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.140
So if you've noticed my summaries are getting better, it's thanks to The Office Bible.
所以如果你发现我的梗概写得越来越好了，那多亏了《办公室》圣经。

66
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.300
Wow.
哇。

67
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.540
How excited were you when you realized there were summaries in there?
当你发现里面有梗概时，你有多兴奋？

68
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.120
You must have been so excited.
你一定特别激动吧。

69
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.720
Lady, yes.
女士，没错。

70
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.640
So excited.
太激动了。

71
00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.780
Fast fact number one, this episode was directed by Ken Whittingham.
冷知识第一条，这一集是由肯·惠廷汉执导的。

72
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.820
We've talked a little bit about Ken before.
我们之前聊过一点关于肯的事。

73
00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.140
Ken directed nine episodes of The Office, including this one.
肯执导了九集《办公室》，包括这一集。

74
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.240
And we reached out to him.
我们联系了他。

75
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.040
Yes, and he sent in some audio clips.
是的，他发来了一些音频片段。

76
00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.620
We're really excited to hear him talk about this episode.
我们非常期待听到他谈论这一集。

77
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:51.740
And Jenna, he is going to come on and be a full Zoom guest for Phyllis's wedding.
而且珍娜，他会作为正式的Zoom嘉宾来参加菲利斯的婚礼那一集。

78
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.020
I don't want to get ahead of ourselves, but we're very excited.
我不想操之过急，但我们真的很兴奋。

79
00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.440
Yes, and Phyllis's wedding is such a milestone episode, and so is this.
是的，菲利斯的婚礼是一个里程碑式的剧集，这一集也是。

80
00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.880
We wanted to ask, Ken, what was it like to merge these two worlds?
我们想问问肯，将这两个世界融合在一起是什么感觉？

81
00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.660
And a lot of people wrote in wanting to know,
很多人写信来想知道，

82
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.440
how did they decide where everybody would sit in the office?
他们是怎么决定办公室里每个人的座位的？

83
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.180
Like, if you notice, suddenly the desk pods go from two to three.
比如，如果你注意到了，办公桌的组合突然从两人位变成了三人位。

84
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.140
Yeah.
没错。

85
00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.820
I remember being so happy that Ken was the one directing this,
我记得当时很高兴是肯来执导这一集，

86
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.420
because we already knew Ken really well.
因为我们已经很了解肯了。

87
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.720
We were so comfortable with him.
我们和他在一起感觉很自在。

88
00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.160
And this was big even for the cast, Jenna.
这对演员来说也是件大事，珍娜。

89
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.940
There was a buzz, because we hadn't been around these people.
当时大家都很兴奋，因为我们之前没怎么和这些人接触过。

90
00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:33.400
And, you know, we barely got to see them at table reads and things like that.
你知道，我们在剧本围读之类的场合几乎见不到他们。

91
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.540
So there was a real sort of buzz on set, and I remember being happy that Ken was there,
所以片场确实有一种兴奋感，我记得当时很高兴肯在那里，

92
00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.580
because he's so calm and, like, that he was going to guide us through the merger.
因为他非常冷静，他会引导我们度过这次合并。

93
00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:50.840
Well, here is his audio clip explaining how he and Greg decided where all the new people would sit.
好了，这是他解释他和格雷格如何决定新员工座位的音频片段。

94
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.980
Introducing the characters from the Stanford branch would be very important to establish these characters
介绍来自斯坦福分部的人物非常重要，要确立这些角色，

95
00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.220
and how they interacted with the Scranton employees, their likes and their dislikes for each other.
以及他们如何与斯克兰顿的员工互动，他们彼此喜欢什么，讨厌什么。

96
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.220
I remember Greg Daniels asking me to decide where the new characters would sit and why.
我记得格雷格·丹尼尔斯让我决定新角色坐在哪里以及原因。

97
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.980
So he and I walked to the set, and I laid out where I thought everyone should be.
于是他和我在片场走了一圈，我规划了每个人应该坐的位置。

98
00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:14.160
Since Ryan had taken Jim's old desk, I decided that Jim would sit directly across from Dwight,
由于瑞安占了吉姆原来的座位，我决定让吉姆直接坐在德怀特对面，

99
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.700
which would be fun for Jim and irritating to Dwight.
这对吉姆来说会很有趣，对德怀特来说则很烦人。

100
00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.280
It would also put Jim in the middle of Karen and Pam, which would also make Jim uncomfortable,
这也会把吉姆夹在凯伦和帕姆中间，这也会让吉姆感到不自在。

101
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.900
and Pam to be able to check out interactions between him and Karen.
以及让帕姆能观察到他和凯伦之间的互动。

102
00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:31.700
I set Andy in between Kevin and Angela to establish Andy's instant attraction to Angela,
我把安迪安排在凯文和安吉拉中间，是为了建立安迪对安吉拉的一见钟情，

103
00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:35.580
and also they would be in Dwight's eyeline to create Dwight's jealousy.
同时也让他们处于德怀特的视线范围内，从而引发德怀特的嫉妒。

104
00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.640
Andy would later move on to Karen's desk.
安迪后来会搬到凯伦的办公桌旁。

105
00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:46.120
I placed Tony in the back near Toby at a very obscure desk because he would be quitting or getting fired in that episode.
我把托尼安排在后面靠近托比的一个很不显眼的位子上，因为他在那一集里会辞职或被解雇。

106
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:53.060
We also discussed how important it was to build Pam's awareness that Jim had moved on and was interested in Karen.
我们还讨论了让帕姆意识到吉姆已经放下过去并对凯伦感兴趣，这一点有多重要。

107
00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.200
I love how much thought went into where everyone sat.
我喜欢大家在座位安排上投入了这么多心思。

108
00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.620
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

109
00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.860
I love the idea of, depending on which character, who could see who, right?
我喜欢这种构思，根据不同角色，谁能看到谁，对吧？

110
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:05.360
Yes.
是的。

111
00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.080
Yeah.
没错。

112
00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.620
And thinking about it from Pam's perspective, and I remember sitting at the desk,
从帕姆的角度去思考，我记得当时坐在那张桌子前，

113
00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:15.900
and there's even a moment in the episode when Pam realizes she's not going to be able to see Jim's face anymore.
剧里甚至有一个瞬间，帕姆意识到她再也看不到吉姆的脸了。

114
00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:16.560
Yeah.
是啊。

115
00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.260
There's a whole deleted scene about that, lady, where you actually come up to him,
关于这一点有一个完整的删减片段，女士，你实际上走到他面前，

116
00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.400
and you're like, this is kind of weird.
然后你说，这感觉有点怪。

117
00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.100
I just stare at your back now.
我现在只能盯着你的后背看。

118
00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.620
It's, really?
真的吗？

119
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:25.670
Yeah.
是啊。

120
00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.300
It's a great deleted scene.
那是一个很棒的删减片段。

121
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:31.700
And you and Jim start doing a bit, and then Ryan's like, can you guys stop?
你和吉姆开始演一段戏，然后瑞安说，你们能停一下吗？

122
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.160
I'm just trying to get some work done.
我只是想把工作做完。

123
00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.600
It's really awkward.
那真的很尴尬。

124
00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.160
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

125
00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.740
I want to go back and see that.
我想回去看看那个片段。

126
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:37.340
Yeah.
好啊。

127
00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:44.780
Because also, after I heard Ken's clip, I was thinking about how, wow, so now Pam can see Karen's face.
因为在听了肯的片段后，我也在想，哇，现在帕姆能看到凯伦的脸了。

128
00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:52.780
So if Karen is making flirty googly eyes at Jim or something, she doesn't know if Jim is reciprocating or not,
所以如果凯伦对吉姆暗送秋波什么的，帕姆不知道吉姆有没有回应，

129
00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.700
because she can only see the back of his head.
因为她只能看到他的后脑勺。

130
00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:55.500
Yeah.
没错。

131
00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:03.240
So in terms of Pam trying to track this relationship going forward, she's only going to have that one thing she can see.
所以就帕姆试图追踪这段关系的发展而言，她只能看到那一点点信息。

132
00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:08.800
It's just, I just love, I love all the thought that goes into these choices.
我只是，我真的很喜欢这些选择背后所投入的所有思考。

133
00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:09.960
Yes.
是的。

134
00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:15.620
And some people I saw wrote in and asked, why would Andy sit in Oscar's desk and where is Oscar?
我看到有些人写信问，为什么安迪会坐在奥斯卡的位子上，奥斯卡去哪了？

135
00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.920
But you have to remember, Oscar is on his paid vacation leave.
但你得记住，奥斯卡正在休带薪假。

136
00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:19.500
Yeah.
是啊。

137
00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.920
So his desk was available.
所以他的位子是空出来的。

138
00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:21.700
Yeah.
没错。

139
00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:29.300
Although, I will say this, Angela, someone wrote in to note that the character of Hannah is technically an accountant.
不过，安吉拉，我要说的是，有人写信指出汉娜这个角色在设定上是会计。

140
00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.000
Oh.
哦。

141
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:31.840
Yeah.
是啊。

142
00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.640
So maybe.
所以也许吧。

143
00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.900
Maybe that's another layer why my character feels so threatened by her.
也许这就是为什么我的角色会觉得她很有威胁感的另一个层面原因。

144
00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:36.500
Yeah.
没错。

145
00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:37.300
Exactly.
正是如此。

146
00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.280
There can only be one bitch in accounting.
会计部只能有一个贱人。

147
00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.700
All right.
好吧。

148
00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.780
Well, I loved that.
嗯，我很喜欢这个。

149
00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.340
Let's move on to fastback number two.
让我们进入第二个快问快答。

150
00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.660
This is the first episode featuring writer Brent Forrester.
这是编剧布伦特·福雷斯特参与的第一集。

151
00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:50.980
Yes.
是的。

152
00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.220
And Brent also sent in audio clips.
布伦特也发来了音频片段。

153
00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.560
We asked him a lot of questions and he sent in clips as well.
我们问了他很多问题，他也发来了片段。

154
00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:03.760
So all throughout this episode, you guys, we're going to have clips from Ken, the director, and Brent, the writer, which is just so fun.
所以在这整集节目里，大家，我们都会穿插导演肯和编剧布伦特发来的片段，这真的太有趣了。

155
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.340
Yeah.
没错。

156
00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.400
I love getting to have those different perspectives.
我喜欢能听到这些不同的视角。

157
00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:13.680
So Angela, you asked Brent about what it was like for him to write his first episode.
安吉拉，你问了布伦特他第一次写剧本是什么感觉。

158
00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:14.420
Yeah.
是的。

159
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.540
This was his first episode and it's such a huge one.
这是他写的第一集，而且是非常重要的一集。

160
00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.820
I was like, Brent, that feels very intimidating.
我就说，布伦特，这感觉太吓人了。

161
00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:23.080
You know, you're writing the merger of Scranton and Stanford.
你知道，你要写的是斯克兰顿和斯坦福分公司的合并。

162
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.180
What was that like?
那是什么感觉？

163
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:24.600
Yeah.
是啊。

164
00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.380
And this is what he had to say.
这是他当时说的话。

165
00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.440
Hi, I'm Brent Forrester, the author of The Merger.
大家好，我是布伦特·福雷斯特，《合并》一集的编剧。

166
00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.960
I was not part of the original writing staff of The Office.
我并不是《办公室》最初编剧团队的一员。

167
00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:41.080
Greg Daniels, the show creator, was a writer with me on The Simpsons and he had me as a writer on King of the Hill.
该剧的创作者格雷格·丹尼尔斯曾和我一起在《辛普森一家》担任编剧，后来在《乡巴佬希尔》中也让我担任了编剧。

168
00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.120
He brought me in in season three.
他在第三季时把我招了进来。

169
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:52.020
And what I remember most about writing this draft was how I totally failed in the first draft to capture the tone of The Office.
关于写这一集初稿，我印象最深的就是我完全没能把握住《办公室》的基调，简直是一败涂地。

170
00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.300
I was trying so hard to be funny.
我当时太努力想写得好笑了。

171
00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.660
I wrote witticisms for every character in The Office every time they opened their mouth.
我给《办公室》里的每个角色都写了俏皮话，只要他们一开口就是。

172
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.480
And Greg was so horrified.
格雷格当时都被吓坏了。

173
00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:09.820
He made Mike Schur, Jen Salata, and Paul Lieberstein, the three senior writers on the show, sit me down and explain to me the tone of The Office,
他让迈克·舒尔、简·萨拉塔和保罗·李伯斯坦这三位剧组资深编剧坐下来，给我讲解《办公室》的基调，

174
00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:17.420
which is the tone of naturalism, where we don't require characters to be saying funny things all the time,
也就是自然主义的基调，我们不需要角色时刻都在说好笑的话，

175
00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:23.700
where we let things be dramatic for long stretches, and where we get comedy from performance above all.
我们让剧情在很长一段时间内保持戏剧性，而且喜剧效果主要来源于表演。

176
00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:37.020
Well, I transformed as a writer between draft one and two of The Merger, and I learned the tone of The Office real faSt.
嗯，在《合并》这一集的第一稿和第二稿之间，我完成了一次蜕变，我很快就掌握了《办公室》的基调。

177
00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:38.780
Oh, Brent.
噢，布伦特。

178
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.480
Don't you love that?
你不觉得这很可爱吗？

179
00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.880
I just love that he was like, yeah, I got it wrong.
我就是喜欢他那种坦诚的态度，说，好吧，我搞砸了。

180
00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:47.260
They kind of like let me know what was what, and then I gave it another try.
他们指点了我一番，然后我又试了一次。

181
00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:53.180
Well, what people should know is that Brent went on to be a co-executive producer of The Office.
嗯，大家应该知道，布伦特后来成为了《办公室》的联合执行制片人。

182
00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.420
He ended up running the show with Paul Lieberstein, so he figured it out.
他最终和保罗·李伯斯坦一起负责这部剧，所以他确实摸透了门道。

183
00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.640
He figured it out.
他摸透了。

184
00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.820
Yeah, he did just fine.
是啊，他做得很好。

185
00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.700
That's right.
没错。

186
00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:01.760
Okay, I'm so excited.
好了，我太兴奋了。

187
00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.300
We're going to have more clips from him coming up, too.
接下来我们还会听到更多他的片段。

188
00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:04.880
Yeah.
没错。

189
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:10.440
Fast fact number three, let's talk about the transfers from Stanford.
冷知识第三条，我们来聊聊从斯坦福调过来的人。

190
00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.720
Yes, Stanford.
是的，斯坦福。

191
00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.420
Here are our new characters.
这是我们的新角色。

192
00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.300
We have Tony Gardner, played by Mike Bruner.
有迈克·布鲁纳饰演的托尼·加德纳。

193
00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:28.500
We have Ursula Burton, who plays Hannah, and we have Wayne Wilderson, who plays Martin Nash.
有饰演汉娜的厄苏拉·伯顿，还有饰演马丁·纳什的韦恩·怀尔德森。

194
00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:35.360
Now, you might recognize Mike Bruner because he did have a small scene with Rashida in an earlier episode.
你们可能认得迈克·布鲁纳，因为他在之前的一集里和拉什达有过一小段对手戏。

195
00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:39.380
Hannah was in the background of a few scenes over in Stanford.
汉娜在斯坦福的几个场景里作为背景出现过。

196
00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:44.480
She had this storyline and some deleted scenes with Jim, but they had been cut.
她原本有一条故事线和一些与吉姆的删减片段，但都被剪掉了。

197
00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:50.700
And then you might recognize Wayne because he had a big recurring role on Veep.
你们可能还认得韦恩，因为他在《副总统》里有一个重要的常驻角色。

198
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.420
And by the way, now he's in Greg's new show, Upload.
顺便说一下，他现在还出演了格雷格的新剧《上载新生》。

199
00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:54.800
Nice.
不错。

200
00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.100
Nice.
不错。

201
00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:00.740
And I want to take a tangent real quickly, Angela, to say that I'm really loving Upload.
安吉拉，我想稍微岔开一下话题，说我真的很喜欢《上载新生》这部剧。

202
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:09.080
It is, I know it's like sci-fi-y, but I'm super digging it because I realized something about my sci-fi thing.
我知道它有点科幻色彩，但我超级喜欢，因为我意识到自己对科幻题材的偏好了。

203
00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:09.820
What?
什么偏好？

204
00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:19.340
Okay, I really like Black Mirror as well, and I feel like Upload has a type of sort of a comedic Black Mirror thing going on.
好吧，我也很喜欢《黑镜》，我觉得《上载新生》有一种类似喜剧版《黑镜》的感觉。

205
00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.880
And is that sci-fi?
那算是科幻吗？

206
00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.600
Is Black Mirror sci-fi fantasy?
《黑镜》属于科幻奇幻类吗？

207
00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.200
Yeah, I would say it is.
是的，我觉得算。

208
00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:32.900
It's a lot of like alternate realities and sort of, yeah, it is.
里面有很多平行现实之类的东西，所以，是的，它算。

209
00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:33.680
I think it is.
我也觉得算。

210
00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:38.420
Okay, is Handmaid's Tale sci-fi fantasy?
那《使女的故事》算科幻奇幻吗？

211
00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.120
See what I'm saying?
明白我的意思了吗？

212
00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.900
This is the category that I like.
这就是我喜欢的类型。

213
00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.480
I like a tiny spin.
我喜欢带点小变数的。

214
00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.300
I love zombie movies.
我喜欢僵尸电影。

215
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.680
I love a tiny...
我喜欢那种小小的……

216
00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.460
I feel like zombie is horror, though.
但我觉得僵尸片属于恐怖片。

217
00:11:50.800 --> 00:12:02.360
I know, but I feel like it's falling in this new category that I want to designate, which is like, it's some of life as we know it and then some new rules.
我知道，但我感觉它属于我想定义的一个新类别，就是那种基于我们已知的现实，但又加入了一些新规则的类型。

218
00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.380
Slightly altered reality.
稍微改变了的现实。

219
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.940
Altered reality.
被改变的现实。

220
00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.640
I'm doing a lot of gestures right now.
我现在手势很多。

221
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:09.120
You are.
确实。

222
00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:10.200
I wish you could see Jenna.
真希望你能看见，珍娜。

223
00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:15.080
She's like cupping the air and then like spinning it over her head like it's a world, a ball.
她刚才双手捧着空气，然后像转动地球仪或球体一样在头顶转动。

224
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.100
I don't know what's happening.
我不知道她在干嘛。

225
00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.660
Right, because this is reality, and then this is altered reality.
对，因为这是现实，而这是被改变的现实。

226
00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.000
Here's the thing, Jenna.
关键是，珍娜。

227
00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.940
Handmaid's Tale, I don't think you can handle it.
《使女的故事》，我觉得你可能受不了。

228
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:23.680
I watched it.
我看过。

229
00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.580
It's fantastic.
太精彩了。

230
00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.880
I couldn't sleep at night.
但我晚上睡不着觉。

231
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:26.820
I was like, oh my gosh.
我当时想，天哪。

232
00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.120
I watched one episode of Handmaid's Tale, and I had nightmares for three nights.
我只看了一集《使女的故事》，结果做了三个晚上的噩梦。

233
00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:32.740
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

234
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.520
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

235
00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:38.220
And I've seen a lot of horror films, but that was, I mean, that got in my head.
我看过很多恐怖片，但那部剧，我是说，它真的钻进我脑子里了。

236
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.320
Holy moly.
天哪。

237
00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.180
Okay, so.
好吧，所以。

238
00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:41.560
But here's what I'm saying.
但我想说的是。

239
00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:45.540
I feel like there is a tangent.
我觉得这算是一个分支。

240
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.580
Here's what I will not let go.
这一点我坚持认为。

241
00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:53.100
I think there's a tangent of sci-fi that I'm super into, and it's altered reality sci-fi.
我觉得科幻里有一个分支是我超级喜欢的，那就是“被改变的现实”类科幻。

242
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.800
Okay, fair enough, lady, fair enough.
好吧，有道理，女士，很有道理。

243
00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:02.000
Also, transfers that you have to mention are Karen Filippelli and Andy Bernard.
另外，必须提到的转职员工还有凯伦·菲利佩利和安迪·伯纳德。

244
00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.120
Oh, my gosh, of course.
天哪，当然了。

245
00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:04.800
Yes.
没错。

246
00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.060
Yes, we have those guys coming over as well.
是的，他们也过来了。

247
00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:14.460
So it's a total of five, a total of five new employees from Stanford that come to Scranton.
所以总共有五个人，总共五名新员工从斯坦福分部调到了斯克兰顿分部。

248
00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:17.720
We had a fan question from a lot of people.
我们收到了很多粉丝的提问。

249
00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:18.260
Okay.
好的。

250
00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:23.060
Jesse Kay, Seth Anderson, Connor McCulloch, and Molly Frank all asked,
杰西·凯、塞斯·安德森、康纳·麦卡洛克和莫莉·弗兰克都问到，

251
00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:28.000
did the writers and cast know that Martin, Hannah, and Tony,
编剧和演员们是否知道马丁、汉娜和托尼，

252
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:33.200
those three of those five transfers, were only temporary characters?
那五个转调员工中的三个，只是临时角色？

253
00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:35.500
Yes, we did.
是的，我们知道。

254
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:36.380
We did.
我们知道。

255
00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:38.620
We didn't know how many episodes, right?
我们当时不知道具体会有多少集，对吧？

256
00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:44.360
But we knew they were going to be part of this new wave that came over that Michael slowly alienates.
但我们知道他们会成为这股新势力的一部分，然后被迈克尔慢慢疏远。

257
00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:51.540
Yes, I remember that there was a conversation that was after the merger, each week,
是的，我记得合并之后有过一次谈话，每周，

258
00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:59.480
one of the new employees would quit until we were just left with Andy and Karen are the two people who would stay.
都会有一名新员工辞职，直到最后只剩下安迪和凯伦留下来。

259
00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:00.280
Yeah.
没错。

260
00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.320
All right, lady,
好了，女士，

261
00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:11.240
maybe we should take a break and then let's get into this episode because I have a big catch right out of the gate in the cold open and I'm really excited to talk about it.
也许我们该休息一下，然后再进入这一集，因为我在冷开场里有个大发现，我真的很兴奋想聊聊它。

262
00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:15.980
All right, we will take a break on that and we will be back with Angela's big catch.
好的，那我们先休息一下，回来后再聊安吉拉的大发现。

263
00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:16.600
Yeah.
好。

264
00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:17.840
Big catch.
大发现。

265
00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:18.980
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

266
00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:31.170
All right, guys, we're back.
好了，各位，我们回来了。

267
00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.490
We start at the Stanford branch.
我们从斯坦福分部开始。

268
00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:34.810
Jim has a talking head.
吉姆有个访谈镜头。

269
00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:37.410
He tells us Stanford branch is closing.
他告诉我们斯坦福分部要关闭了。

270
00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.890
Andy made Stanford RIP hats for everyone.
安迪给每个人都做了“斯坦福安息吧”的帽子。

271
00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.630
Andy asked Jim what Michael Scott is like.
安迪问吉姆迈克尔·斯科特是个什么样的人。

272
00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.110
Yeah, he wants some intel.
没错，他想打听点情报。

273
00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:47.990
He wants some intel.
他想打听点情报。

274
00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.990
He wants to know how to work the system over there.
他想知道在那边该怎么混。

275
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:50.730
Yeah.
是啊。

276
00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.170
And Jim's like, you know what?
吉姆就说，你知道吗？

277
00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:53.850
You just kind of have to meet him.
你得亲自去见见他。

278
00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:55.750
You have to meet him.
你得见见他。

279
00:14:55.930 --> 00:15:01.750
But did you notice when Andy was asking him about Michael, he was like, what kind of magazines does he like?
但你注意到安迪问他关于迈克尔的事时，他问的是，他喜欢什么样的杂志吗？

280
00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:03.030
We know.
我们都知道。

281
00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.490
We know what magazines.
我们知道是什么杂志。

282
00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:05.870
American Way.
《美国航空》杂志。

283
00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:06.790
He loves Trout.
他超爱《鳟鱼》杂志。

284
00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:07.270
Yeah.
没错。

285
00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:08.810
He loves American Way.
他超爱《美国航空》杂志。

286
00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:12.930
If Jim had given Andy the list of magazines, would that have helped, Andy?
如果吉姆给了安迪那份杂志清单，会对安迪有帮助吗？

287
00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:18.810
I feel like if someone gave me Michael's list of magazines, I would be like, I am even more confused about this person.
我觉得如果有人给了我迈克尔的杂志清单，我会觉得，我对这个人更困惑了。

288
00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:19.990
I am intrigued.
我很好奇。

289
00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:21.650
Who is this person?
这人到底是谁？

290
00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:25.550
So then Jim and Karen, they have a little moment.
然后吉姆和凯伦，他们有了个小瞬间。

291
00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.970
They agree this is going to be a big adventure.
他们一致认为这将是一场大冒险。

292
00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:33.270
Karen gives Jim a real flirty flirt look, but Jim doesn't see it, right?
凯伦给了吉姆一个非常调情的眼神，但吉姆没看见，对吧？

293
00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.490
But like she's pining.
但她就像在渴望着什么。

294
00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.470
Her heart is a flutter.
她心潮澎湃。

295
00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:47.850
I feel like Karen flirts and then Jim high fives, which for any woman like that's into a guy, if you flirt a little and like maybe cut some eyes at them and you get a high five,
我觉得凯伦调情，然后吉姆击掌，对于任何对男生有好感的女性来说，如果你调情了一下，甚至可能对他暗送秋波，结果却换来一个击掌，

296
00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:48.230
it's like.
那感觉就像是。

297
00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:52.490
I'm like, Karen, there are so many signs here.
我当时想，凯伦，这里有这么多信号啊。

298
00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.190
Don't do it.
别这样。

299
00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:58.210
We're going to get into something I've started tracking called wishy-washy Jim.
我们要聊聊我开始追踪的一个现象，叫“摇摆不定的吉姆”。

300
00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.470
Oh, well, welcome.
哦，好吧，欢迎。

301
00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:01.710
Welcome to the club.
欢迎加入俱乐部。

302
00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:04.230
I mean, he's been wishy-washy for a long time.
我是说，他一直都优柔寡断的。

303
00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:08.230
Yeah, but he does a lot of super big wishy-washies in this episode.
没错，但他在这一集里表现得特别优柔寡断。

304
00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.050
All right.
好吧。

305
00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:10.950
Now we're back in Scranton.
现在我们回到了斯克兰顿。

306
00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:16.290
Toby has come up to Pam at reception and he's talking about how he completed his run.
托比走到前台找帕姆，说他跑完了步。

307
00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.650
And I have a catch.
而且我有个发现。

308
00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.750
Oh, and is this what you teased us about before the break?
噢，这就是你在休息前卖关子的内容吗？

309
00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.810
This is what I teased you about.
这就是我卖关子的内容。

310
00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.450
It's now I've set it up.
现在我已经铺垫好了。

311
00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:37.450
It is going to be so lame, but at a minute, six seconds, new plant alert, new plant alert at front reception.
这可能会很无聊，但在1分06秒处，新植物警报，前台有新植物警报。

312
00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:45.990
You have a friend in Hadley Locke who wrote in to say, Angela, is that a new tree at Pam's desk?
你的朋友哈德利·洛克写信来说：安吉拉，帕姆桌上那是棵新植物吗？

313
00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.830
Hadley, it is a new plant.
哈德利，那确实是一棵新植物。

314
00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.090
It's in a maroon ceramic pot.
它装在一个栗色的陶瓷盆里。

315
00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:57.630
Like, not just like, usually Pam's plants are just in like that plastic crap that comes from the store.
不像平时帕姆的植物，通常只是装在那种从商店买来的塑料破盆里。

316
00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:58.530
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吗？

317
00:16:58.750 --> 00:16:59.110
Yeah.
懂。

318
00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.030
This isn't an actual pot.
那不是真正的花盆。

319
00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:07.150
But Hadley, my friend Hadley, did you see what happens to the plant later in the episode?
但是哈德利，我的朋友哈德利，你看到这棵植物在这一集后面发生了什么吗？

320
00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.490
What happens?
发生了什么？

321
00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.510
Where's it go?
它去哪儿了？

322
00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:18.410
So, Hadley, did you notice that at a minute, six seconds, there's the one plant, but then go to five minutes, 25 seconds.
所以，哈德利，你注意到在1分06秒时是那棵植物，但到了5分25秒时吗？

323
00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:19.730
It's a totally different plant.
那是完全不同的植物。

324
00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:20.350
What?
什么？

325
00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:24.610
Whatever plant we used in the cold open, I don't know what happened to it.
不管我们在片头冷笑话里用了什么植物，我不知道它后来怎么了。

326
00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:25.590
They couldn't find it.
他们找不到它了。

327
00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.210
Someone got a different plant.
有人拿了另一棵植物来。

328
00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.170
It is a different plant.
那确实是不同的植物。

329
00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:32.950
The plant at a minute, six seconds is like small, light green leaves.
1分06秒时的植物叶子比较小，颜色浅绿。

330
00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:37.350
And then at five minutes, 25, it's the big dark green kind of leaves.
然后到了5分25秒，变成了那种大而深绿的叶子。

331
00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.350
And it's in a different pot holder.
而且它装在不同的花盆里。

332
00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:48.030
It's in like the clay-looking pot holder, whereas at a minute, six seconds, it's like a shiny maroon pot holder.
它装在看起来像陶土的花盆里，而1分06秒时，它装在一个闪亮的栗色花盆里。

333
00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:53.370
Guys, I know this is what you're here for, but this is some serious plant gate.
伙计们，我知道你们就是为了这个来的，但这可是严重的“植物门”事件。

334
00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:54.390
Plant gate.
植物门。

335
00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.850
You have found the evidence for something I was wondering about.
你找到了我一直好奇的事情的证据。

336
00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.730
I think we filmed this cold open on another day.
我想我们是在另一天拍摄这个片头冷笑话的。

337
00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:01.770
Oh.
噢。

338
00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:06.770
I think we inserted this cold open that it wasn't in the original shooting draft.
我想我们是后来插入了这个冷笑话，它不在最初的拍摄剧本里。

339
00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:13.950
So I think we came back and did this whole Dwight-Toby running thing at a different time.
所以我认为我们是回来在不同的时间拍摄了整个德怀特和托比跑步的戏份。

340
00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.790
And that's why the plants are different.
这就是为什么植物不一样。

341
00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.130
Yes, that would make sense.
是的，这说得通。

342
00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:21.330
They knew there was a plant on your desk, but they couldn't get the same one.
他们知道你桌上有棵植物，但他们没能找到同一棵。

343
00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:22.810
So they just had to budget.
所以他们只能凑合了。

344
00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.790
Okay, because here's the thing.
好吧，因为重点是这个。

345
00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.170
Pam takes Dwight down to the parking lot, right?
帕姆带德怀特去了停车场，对吧？

346
00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.530
Because he says that he can run faster than Toby, faster than anything.
因为他说他跑得比托比快，比什么都快。

347
00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.570
He's not impressed with Toby's running time.
他对托比的跑步时间很不屑。

348
00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:38.630
Jenna, he can run faster than a snake, a mongoose, and a panther.
珍娜，他说他跑得比蛇、猫鼬和黑豹还快。

349
00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:39.430
Somewhere in there.
大概就在那附近吧。

350
00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:40.470
That's his speed.
那就是他的速度。

351
00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:41.350
Right.
没错。

352
00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:46.390
So Pam is like, all right, I'm going to time you.
帕姆说，好吧，我要给你计时。

353
00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:49.210
And she makes Dwight run around the building.
然后她让德怀特绕着大楼跑。

354
00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.990
She's holding a digital thermometer.
她手里拿着一个数字温度计。

355
00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:55.650
She has this sort of long, kind of sort of a talking head.
她有一段挺长的，算是那种面对镜头的独白。

356
00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.770
She's kind of talking out loud, talking to the documentary crew.
她在那儿自言自语，对着纪录片摄制组说话。

357
00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:00.830
And then she just goes inside.
然后她就直接进去了。

358
00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:01.890
She abandons Dwight.
她把德怀特抛下了。

359
00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:07.070
We had fan questions from Spencer Brandon, Mateus Almeida, and Angie T.
我们收到了来自Spencer Brandon、Mateus Almeida和Angie T.的粉丝提问。

360
00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:11.530
Does Rain actually run around the whole building in the cold open?
雷恩在片头真的绕着整栋大楼跑了吗？

361
00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:16.470
How did they time it out for Dwight to be running around the corner just as Pam finished talking?
他们是怎么掌握时间的，让德怀特刚好在帕姆说完话时转过拐角？

362
00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.030
All right, Angela, I watched this scene.
好吧，安吉拉，我看了这一幕。

363
00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:23.190
It is a one shot.
这是一个长镜头。

364
00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:24.610
There is no cut.
没有剪辑。

365
00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.050
So did Rain really have to run around the building?
所以雷恩真的必须绕着大楼跑吗？

366
00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:31.430
Well, you reached out to Ken Whittingham, right?
嗯，你联系了肯·惠廷汉姆，对吧？

367
00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.010
I did.
是的。

368
00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:33.630
And you asked him what he remembered.
你问他记不记得这件事。

369
00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:38.310
And he said he did not film this cold open.
他说他没拍这个片头。

370
00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:43.470
No, which, again, is further evidence to you that we filmed it on a different day.
没错，这再次证明了我们是在不同的一天拍摄的。

371
00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:47.390
So someone else had to direct just this cold open because it was an insert, right?
所以一定有别人执导了这个片头，因为它是个插曲，对吧？

372
00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:48.370
Yes.
是的。

373
00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:52.310
I was trying to remember shooting this scene.
我试着回忆拍摄这一幕的情景。

374
00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:58.470
And I have a memory that, yes, the reason I'm talking kind of so slowly is because Rain
我记得，没错，我说话之所以这么慢，是因为雷恩

375
00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:00.210
really had to run.
真的得跑。

376
00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:04.150
Yet at the same time, I didn't think he ran around the whole building.
但同时，我不觉得他绕着整栋大楼跑了。

377
00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:07.130
So I reached out to Rain.
所以我联系了雷恩。

378
00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.510
And?
然后呢？

379
00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.510
Rain said he cut through the warehouse.
雷恩说他穿过了仓库。

380
00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:13.970
Oh, that's smart.
哦，那很聪明。

381
00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:20.730
So if you notice, the camera pans to me and he cut through the warehouse, through the building,
如果你注意看，镜头转向我时，他穿过了仓库，穿过大楼，

382
00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.810
to the door on the other side, and then he ran around the corner.
到了另一边的门，然后他才绕过拐角。

383
00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:27.430
So he was still running a significant amount.
所以他跑的距离还是相当长的。

384
00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:34.710
Here's what I also thought when I watched that is, once again, Pam has become the gem of this
我看完那一幕还想到一点，帕姆再次成为了这个

385
00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.110
office.
办公室的瑰宝。

386
00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:36.830
She's the prankster now.
她现在成了恶作剧者。

387
00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.650
She's timing him with a thermometer, making him run around the building.
她用温度计给他计时，让他绕着大楼跑。

388
00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.090
Pam is Jim.
帕姆就是吉姆。

389
00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:47.090
Oh, I bet she can't wait to tell Jim what she did when he finally gets there.
哦，我敢说她等不及要告诉吉姆她做了什么，等他终于到那儿的时候。

390
00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.010
Too bad.
太可惜了。

391
00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.310
He's not going to want to hang out with her.
他不会想和她待在一起的。

392
00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:49.610
Sorry.
抱歉。

393
00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:50.670
He doesn't engage.
他不参与。

394
00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.870
Well, we'll get to that.
嗯，我们之后会讲到。

395
00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:52.710
We'll get to that.
我们之后会讲到。

396
00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:53.230
All right.
好吧。

397
00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.150
So now, here it is.
那么现在，开始了。

398
00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:58.810
Dwight and Michael, they're prepping the office for the new arrivals.
德怀特和迈克尔，他们正在为新人的到来布置办公室。

399
00:20:59.010 --> 00:20:59.570
They're going around.
他们四处走动。

400
00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.470
They're putting name tags for everyone.
他们正在为每个人贴上名牌。

401
00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.350
There's gift bags.
有礼品袋。

402
00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:09.110
I have to think the party planning committee had to stuff those bags with pencils and coupons.
我觉得礼品袋肯定是派对策划委员会往里面塞了铅笔和优惠券。

403
00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:14.350
You know, I wanted to discuss the gift bags, Angela, because I thought they were a really
安吉拉，我想聊聊礼品袋的事，因为我觉得它们真的是

404
00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:15.070
nice gesture.
一种很好的心意。

405
00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.030
I think they are, too.
我也这么觉得。

406
00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:23.030
I, you know, I sort of appreciate we have to go out of town a lot, right, for work.
你知道，我很感激我们经常要出差，对吧，为了工作。

407
00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:29.210
And I always appreciate when the film company or the television company, they'll put like
而且我总是很感激电影公司或电视公司，他们会放一个

408
00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:35.910
a little binder full of local restaurants and attractions for me to thumb through as
装满当地餐馆和景点的小活页夹，让我翻阅，因为

409
00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:40.010
I am now about to spend two months in this location that I don't know.
我马上要在这样一个我不熟悉的地方待上两个月。

410
00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:45.870
I think it's lovely to offer people little local coupons, suggestions of where to eat.
我觉得给人们提供一些当地优惠券和用餐建议真的很贴心。

411
00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:48.130
Very thoughtful nifty, gifty bag.
非常周到、精巧的礼品袋。

412
00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:53.450
I'm the type of person, if I check into a hotel and they give me a bottled water, I'm like,
我是那种人，如果我入住酒店，他们给我一瓶水，我会说，

413
00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:54.310
thank you.
谢谢。

414
00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:55.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

415
00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:57.290
I love small gestures.
我喜欢这些小举动。

416
00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:58.870
And I think this is really sweet.
我觉得这真的很贴心。

417
00:21:59.130 --> 00:21:59.930
I do, too.
我也是。

418
00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:03.690
And I feel like it just doesn't get the sort of appreciation that it should.
我觉得它没有得到应有的赞赏。

419
00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:04.870
The nifty, gifty bag.
那个精巧的礼品袋。

420
00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:06.490
I thought it was very thoughtful of Michael.
我觉得迈克尔非常有心。

421
00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:10.470
Also, I want to start using nifty, gifty.
另外，我想开始用“精巧礼品”这个词。

422
00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:13.370
That is a fantastic phrase.
那真是一个绝妙的短语。

423
00:22:13.570 --> 00:22:14.530
Nifty, gifties.
精巧礼品。

424
00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:16.330
Nifty, gifties.
精巧礼品。

425
00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:17.330
Nifty, gifties.
精巧礼品。

426
00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:17.690
Okay.
好的。

427
00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:23.730
So as they're walking around prepping the office, Dwight suggests Michael fire Anthony Gardner
当他们在办公室走动准备时，德怀特建议迈克尔在中午之前解雇安东尼·加德纳

428
00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.290
before noon to consolidate power.
以巩固权力。

429
00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:28.830
But Michael's like, I'm not going to do that, Dwight.
但迈克尔说，我不会那么做的，德怀特。

430
00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:30.250
I'm not going to do that.
我不会那么做的。

431
00:22:31.170 --> 00:22:32.870
But he's planting the seeds.
但他正在埋下种子。

432
00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:34.110
Someone must go today.
今天必须有人走。

433
00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:34.710
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:37.810
Okay, so at four minutes, Pam enters in.
好的，在四分钟的时候，帕姆进来了。

435
00:22:37.930 --> 00:22:38.970
She's carrying food.
她提着食物。

436
00:22:39.390 --> 00:22:41.770
Michael asked her to set it all up in the conference room.
迈克尔让她把所有东西都在会议室布置好。

437
00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:45.490
Jenna, you're holding two really big grocery bags.
珍娜，你手里提着两个非常大的购物袋。

438
00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:46.010
Yeah.
是啊。

439
00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:51.630
And I have what I'm going to start calling a random prop alert.
我有一个要开始称之为“随机道具警报”的东西。

440
00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:52.410
Yep.
没错。

