他列出了他的行动计划。

598
00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:24.250
Here's what it includes.
内容如下。

599
00:29:25.950 --> 00:29:30.170
Repetition, personality mirroring, and never breaking off a handshake.
重复、模仿对方性格，以及握手时绝不先松开。

600
00:29:30.910 --> 00:29:35.130
He says you always have to think one step ahead like a carpenter who makes stairs.
他说你必须时刻领先一步，就像做楼梯的木匠一样。

601
00:29:35.950 --> 00:29:37.310
I want to discuss this.
我想讨论一下这件事。

602
00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:39.490
I think this is a really good strategy.
我觉得这真的是个好策略。

603
00:29:41.090 --> 00:29:42.570
I kind of want to try it.
我有点想试试。

604
00:29:43.790 --> 00:29:44.930
No, no, Jenna.
不，不，珍娜。

605
00:29:45.110 --> 00:29:46.470
I don't see this going well.
我觉得这不会有好结果。

606
00:29:46.670 --> 00:29:46.950
Don't.
别这样。

607
00:29:47.050 --> 00:29:47.770
I don't know.
我不知道。

608
00:29:47.930 --> 00:29:53.090
You can't like walk up to someone and just start imitating how they talk and their movements.
你不能直接走到别人面前，就开始模仿他们的说话方式和动作。

609
00:29:53.530 --> 00:29:54.450
I don't know.
我不知道。

610
00:29:54.670 --> 00:29:58.790
I mean, I think it's personality mirroring.
我是说，我觉得这叫个性镜像。

611
00:29:58.890 --> 00:30:00.150
Is that an actual thing?
真有这种说法吗？

612
00:30:00.390 --> 00:30:02.910
Is that taught at leadership seminars somewhere?
这是哪里的领导力研讨会教的吗？

613
00:30:02.910 --> 00:30:08.030
Because it feels this feels very much like Andy went to a leadership seminar and they're
因为这感觉，这感觉太像安迪去参加了什么领导力研讨会，然后他们

614
00:30:08.030 --> 00:30:09.910
like, here's how you make a good first impression.
告诉他，这是给人留下好第一印象的方法。

615
00:30:10.190 --> 00:30:11.790
Say their name a whole bunch.
多叫几次对方的名字。

616
00:30:12.170 --> 00:30:12.310
Yeah.
是啊。

617
00:30:12.470 --> 00:30:13.230
Name repetition.
重复名字。

618
00:30:14.490 --> 00:30:15.910
Never break a handshake.
握手永远别松开。

619
00:30:16.110 --> 00:30:17.270
I don't know, Ange.
我不知道，安吉拉。

620
00:30:17.430 --> 00:30:18.230
Can we try it?
我们能试一下吗？

621
00:30:18.310 --> 00:30:19.010
I'm going to meet you.
我来和你见个面。

622
00:30:19.170 --> 00:30:19.450
Okay.
好。

623
00:30:19.850 --> 00:30:20.490
Go ahead.
开始吧。

624
00:30:20.690 --> 00:30:21.550
I'm going to be Andy.
我来扮演安迪。

625
00:30:21.750 --> 00:30:21.850
Go.
开始。

626
00:30:23.450 --> 00:30:23.930
Hi.
嗨。

627
00:30:24.390 --> 00:30:24.870
Hey.
嘿。

628
00:30:25.290 --> 00:30:26.170
How are you?
你好吗？

629
00:30:26.410 --> 00:30:27.070
I'm good.
我很好。

630
00:30:27.070 --> 00:30:27.930
How are you, Angela?
你好吗，安吉拉？

631
00:30:28.710 --> 00:30:31.150
I haven't told you my name yet, creeper.
我还没告诉你我叫什么名字呢，变态。

632
00:30:31.150 --> 00:30:34.130
Or how'd you know it was me?
或者你怎么知道是我？

633
00:30:34.490 --> 00:30:35.890
Have you been stalking me?
你一直在跟踪我吗？

634
00:30:36.270 --> 00:30:36.750
Psycho.
神经病。

635
00:30:37.270 --> 00:30:38.910
I Googled you before our meeting.
我在开会前谷歌过你。

636
00:30:39.250 --> 00:30:39.730
Okay.
好吧。

637
00:30:39.930 --> 00:30:40.210
I'm out.
我不干了。

638
00:30:40.210 --> 00:30:40.990
This is not going well.
这进展得不顺利。

639
00:30:41.230 --> 00:30:41.770
I'm out.
我不干了。

640
00:30:41.870 --> 00:30:42.650
I failed.
我失败了。

641
00:30:43.190 --> 00:30:44.430
I did a terrible job.
我表现得太糟糕了。

642
00:30:44.450 --> 00:30:45.790
You failed in three sentences.
你三句话就搞砸了。

643
00:30:46.450 --> 00:30:47.170
Oh, boy.
天哪。

644
00:30:47.290 --> 00:30:47.530
All right.
好吧。

645
00:30:47.670 --> 00:30:48.150
Maybe not.
也许不行。

646
00:30:48.430 --> 00:30:48.630
Okay.
好吧。

647
00:30:49.090 --> 00:30:49.390
Okay.
好吧。

648
00:30:49.570 --> 00:30:50.510
So Andy arrives.
所以安迪到了。

649
00:30:50.750 --> 00:30:56.210
He gets his nifty gifties and he does his strategy and Michael loves it.
他带着他的精美小礼物，使出了他的策略，迈克尔很喜欢。

650
00:30:56.930 --> 00:30:57.410
Yes.
是的。

651
00:30:57.490 --> 00:31:00.650
Michael thinks he's awesome because Andy is doing an impression of Michael.
迈克尔觉得他很了不起，因为安迪在模仿他。

652
00:31:00.650 --> 00:31:03.650
So Michael probably feels like he gets me.
所以迈克尔大概觉得他很懂我。

653
00:31:04.070 --> 00:31:04.230
Yeah.
是啊。

654
00:31:04.390 --> 00:31:04.990
He loves it.
他很喜欢这样。

655
00:31:05.070 --> 00:31:06.430
We had a fan catch, Angela.
我们刚才接住了一个飞球，安吉拉。

656
00:31:06.730 --> 00:31:06.970
Oh.
哦。

657
00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:13.570
Veronica Ramirez noted that when Andy was in the parking lot doing his talking head, he
维罗妮卡·拉米雷斯指出，当安迪在停车场录制访谈时，他

658
00:31:13.570 --> 00:31:15.510
has his tan jacket on.
穿着那件棕褐色夹克。

659
00:31:15.630 --> 00:31:16.050
Yeah.
没错。

660
00:31:16.130 --> 00:31:19.450
But when he walks through the door, it's nowhere to be seen.
但当他走进门时，夹克却不见了。

661
00:31:20.050 --> 00:31:20.550
Oh.
哦。

662
00:31:20.610 --> 00:31:22.230
Where did he take off his jacket?
他是在哪儿脱掉夹克的？

663
00:31:22.470 --> 00:31:23.590
Where did he put his jacket?
他把夹克放哪儿了？

664
00:31:24.210 --> 00:31:26.310
He left it with that other plant.
他把它和另一盆植物放在一起了。

665
00:31:26.970 --> 00:31:27.670
He did.
确实。

666
00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:29.430
They're in a warehouse somewhere.
它们现在在仓库的某个地方。

667
00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:31.670
It's like in a box of lost things.
就像在一个失物招领箱里一样。

668
00:31:32.170 --> 00:31:32.650
Yeah.
是啊。

669
00:31:33.150 --> 00:31:34.590
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

670
00:31:34.810 --> 00:31:37.750
Guess who's making his big debut?
猜猜谁要隆重登场了？

671
00:31:38.590 --> 00:31:38.790
Jim.
吉姆。

672
00:31:39.290 --> 00:31:40.570
He walks in with Martin.
他和马丁一起走了进来。

673
00:31:41.110 --> 00:31:42.150
They're talking sports.
他们在聊体育。

674
00:31:42.790 --> 00:31:46.990
Pam about does a cartwheel to get to him.
帕姆简直要翻个跟头冲过去找他。

675
00:31:47.230 --> 00:31:48.550
And hugs him.
还拥抱了他。

676
00:31:48.990 --> 00:31:50.890
Leaps into his arms, really.
准确说是跳进了他的怀里。

677
00:31:51.190 --> 00:31:51.370
Yeah.
没错。

678
00:31:51.490 --> 00:31:53.630
I was going to say, this is not just a hug.
我正想说，这可不仅仅是个拥抱。

679
00:31:53.910 --> 00:31:56.550
She throws herself on him.
她整个人都扑向了他。

680
00:31:56.910 --> 00:31:57.390
Yeah.
是啊。

681
00:31:57.390 --> 00:31:59.030
But can I say something?
但我能说点什么吗？

682
00:31:59.730 --> 00:32:00.310
Say it.
说吧。

683
00:32:00.550 --> 00:32:02.270
It's seven minutes, 27 seconds.
那是七分二十七秒的时候。

684
00:32:02.610 --> 00:32:04.690
I have a giant zit next to my chin.
我下巴旁边长了一个巨大的痘痘。

685
00:32:05.190 --> 00:32:07.290
And they have tried to cover it up.
他们试着把它遮住。

686
00:32:07.810 --> 00:32:13.470
But it's like a little bit like when you try to cover up like super big zits.
但这就像你试图遮住那种超大痘痘时的感觉。

687
00:32:13.550 --> 00:32:14.610
This is one of those zits.
这就是那种痘痘之一。

688
00:32:14.970 --> 00:32:18.290
And I honestly remember it, believe it or not.
信不信由你，我真的还记得它。

689
00:32:18.410 --> 00:32:21.430
And when I saw it, I was like, oh, yeah, I remember that.
当我看到的时候，我就想，噢，对，我记得那个。

690
00:32:21.430 --> 00:32:25.990
It was it's one of those zits that feels like it's throbbing on your face.
它就是那种感觉在脸上突突跳动的痘痘。

691
00:32:26.250 --> 00:32:26.410
Yeah.
是啊。

692
00:32:26.710 --> 00:32:28.190
It's a zit that has a heartbeat.
那是一个有心跳的痘痘。

693
00:32:28.470 --> 00:32:29.250
That's what I call it.
我是这么叫它的。

694
00:32:29.270 --> 00:32:29.810
It has a heartbeat.
它有心跳。

695
00:32:30.070 --> 00:32:33.330
And you can't squeeze it because it's so underground.
而且你没法挤它，因为它长在皮下深处。

696
00:32:33.950 --> 00:32:37.870
But it's like a beacon shining off your face.
但它就像你脸上的一个发光信号灯。

697
00:32:38.570 --> 00:32:40.110
And here it was.
而它当时就在那儿。

698
00:32:40.270 --> 00:32:44.190
We had to film this scene where Pam is going to see Jim for the first time.
我们当时得拍这场戏，帕姆第一次去见吉姆。

699
00:32:44.390 --> 00:32:48.490
And I was like, I cannot believe we're dealing with this today.
我当时心想，真不敢相信我们今天得应付这个。

700
00:32:48.830 --> 00:32:51.790
And the makeup department, I mean, they did their beSt.
化妆部门，我是说，他们已经尽力了。

701
00:32:51.990 --> 00:32:54.310
They caked a bunch of makeup on it.
他们在上面涂了厚厚一层妆。

702
00:32:54.310 --> 00:32:55.430
But it is there.
但它还是在那儿。

703
00:32:55.430 --> 00:32:56.090
There's only so much you can do.
能做的也就这么多了。

704
00:32:56.330 --> 00:32:57.490
There's only so much.
也就只能做这么多了。

705
00:32:57.810 --> 00:32:58.790
And it's there.
而且它还在那儿。

706
00:32:59.030 --> 00:32:59.370
Yeah.
是啊。

707
00:32:59.650 --> 00:33:01.750
And it still bums me out today.
直到今天它还是让我很沮丧。

708
00:33:01.990 --> 00:33:02.930
It's OK, lady.
没事的，女士。

709
00:33:03.070 --> 00:33:04.890
I had a big zit in the Valentine's episode.
在情人节那一集里，我长了个大痘痘。

710
00:33:05.110 --> 00:33:07.310
And all the photos we took, remember we did?
还有我们拍的所有照片，记得吗？

711
00:33:07.370 --> 00:33:08.810
It was like a whole first photo day.
那就像是专门的第一次拍照日。

712
00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:13.250
There's like photos of me looking up at Dwight, this like Valentine's photo.
照片里我抬头看着德怀特，就像这种情人节照片。

713
00:33:13.290 --> 00:33:14.310
And I have an enormous zit.
而且我长了个巨大的痘痘。

714
00:33:14.950 --> 00:33:16.250
So, you know.
所以，你知道的。

715
00:33:16.650 --> 00:33:18.630
I can't remember what episode it is.
我不记得是哪一集了。

716
00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:24.250
But I'm going to ask Greg because there was a future episode that was like a huge Jim Pam thing.
但我打算问问格雷格，因为后来有一集是关于吉姆和帕姆的大事件。

717
00:33:24.250 --> 00:33:27.250
And I had another one of these big zits.
当时我又长了这么大一颗痘痘。

718
00:33:28.090 --> 00:33:30.510
And then when I saw the episode, it was gone.
然后当我看到那一集时，它不见了。

719
00:33:30.510 --> 00:33:34.030
And I swear, I was like, Greg, what happened?
我发誓，我当时就问，格雷格，发生了什么？

720
00:33:34.150 --> 00:33:35.310
He said, you know what, Jenna?
他说，你知道吗，珍娜？

721
00:33:35.510 --> 00:33:37.390
We decided to take it out in poSt.
我们决定在后期把它处理掉。

722
00:33:37.650 --> 00:33:41.230
We CGI'd your zit away because it was really distracting.
我们用电脑特效把你的痘痘去掉了，因为它真的很抢镜。

723
00:33:42.390 --> 00:33:47.190
How embarrassing, Jenna, that there was a room full of people that you didn't even know
真尴尬啊，珍娜，居然有一屋子你都不认识的人

724
00:33:47.190 --> 00:33:53.390
who had to have a conversation about, do we have it in the budget to scoochie out her zit
专门讨论说，我们的预算够不够把她的痘痘给修掉

725
00:33:53.390 --> 00:33:55.590
in like post-edit?
在后期剪辑里？

726
00:33:55.770 --> 00:34:00.810
And then it was someone's job to painstakingly remove it frame by frame.
然后还得有人负责一帧一帧地把它辛苦修掉。

727
00:34:01.010 --> 00:34:01.410
Yeah.
是啊。

728
00:34:01.650 --> 00:34:03.130
It was so distracting.
它确实太抢镜了。

729
00:34:03.690 --> 00:34:04.510
Oh, Lord.
天哪。

730
00:34:04.910 --> 00:34:06.410
Well, Jenna, you're not alone.
好吧，珍娜，你并不孤单。

731
00:34:06.870 --> 00:34:10.510
Hadley, who also noticed the plant, wrote in and said,
哈德利也注意到了那盆植物，他写信来说，

732
00:34:11.090 --> 00:34:13.350
at the talking head at 3 minutes 55 seconds,
在3分55秒的采访镜头里，

733
00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:16.710
does Dwight have a little pimple on his right cheek?
德怀特的右脸颊上是不是有个小痘痘？

734
00:34:16.710 --> 00:34:21.330
Like, why were we all so pimply in this episode?
话说，为什么我们这一集里都长了痘痘？

735
00:34:21.690 --> 00:34:22.790
Was it the summer?
是因为夏天吗？

736
00:34:22.970 --> 00:34:24.210
Were we just all hot and sweaty?
是因为我们当时都又热又出汗吗？

737
00:34:24.590 --> 00:34:25.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

738
00:34:25.650 --> 00:34:26.430
Maybe so.
也许吧。

739
00:34:26.810 --> 00:34:27.310
All right.
好吧。

740
00:34:27.930 --> 00:34:32.330
So Jim now enters and Dwight and Jim are reunited.
现在吉姆进来了，德怀特和吉姆重聚了。

741
00:34:32.770 --> 00:34:36.550
Jim messes with Dwight immediately by pretending like he's meeting his eyeline,
吉姆立刻开始捉弄德怀特，假装在和他对视，

742
00:34:36.750 --> 00:34:37.610
even though he's not.
尽管他其实并没有。

743
00:34:37.890 --> 00:34:38.130
Yeah.
是啊。

744
00:34:38.310 --> 00:34:39.950
Jim and Dwight are right back at it.
吉姆和德怀特又开始斗智斗勇了。

745
00:34:39.950 --> 00:34:47.150
And if you guys love to track a really good John Krasinski, Dwight, go to 7 minutes 53 seconds.
如果你们喜欢捕捉约翰·卡拉辛斯基和德怀特的精彩互动，请看7分53秒。

746
00:34:47.530 --> 00:34:48.250
Oh, nice.
哦，不错。

747
00:34:48.250 --> 00:34:49.590
It's a really good, hi, Dwight.
那是一个非常棒的“嗨，德怀特”。

748
00:34:50.090 --> 00:34:50.650
Nice.
不错。

749
00:34:51.470 --> 00:34:55.370
So everyone has arrived now, and we had a fan question.
现在所有人都到齐了，我们有一个粉丝提问。

750
00:34:55.650 --> 00:34:56.730
A lot of people wrote in.
很多人都写信来问。

751
00:34:56.910 --> 00:35:02.070
Kristen F., Sarah Hodges, Connor McCulloch, Erica Sansom, and more,
克里斯汀·F、莎拉·霍奇斯、康纳·麦卡洛克、埃里卡·桑瑟姆等人，

752
00:35:02.290 --> 00:35:07.710
all wanted to know what was it like having all these new actors on set from the Stanford branch?
都想知道，片场来了这么多斯坦福分公司的新演员是什么感觉？

753
00:35:07.710 --> 00:35:10.590
And what was it like to have John back?
还有，约翰回来是什么感觉？

754
00:35:11.070 --> 00:35:12.930
I wrote about this in my journal.
我在日记里写过这个。

755
00:35:13.170 --> 00:35:14.330
Of course you did.
你当然写了。

756
00:35:14.590 --> 00:35:16.170
Of course you journaled this.
你当然会把这事记在日记里。

757
00:35:16.430 --> 00:35:17.190
I said,
我说，

758
00:35:17.330 --> 00:35:20.430
We were really excited to shoot the merger.
我们当时真的很兴奋能拍合并的那一集。

759
00:35:20.610 --> 00:35:22.270
It was like we were meeting new people.
感觉就像在结识新朋友一样。

760
00:35:22.470 --> 00:35:26.030
The Stanford and Scranton branches shot on different days and different sound stages,
斯坦福和斯克兰顿分公司是在不同的日子、不同的摄影棚拍摄的，

761
00:35:26.030 --> 00:35:30.290
so we almost never were together except for maybe just a few times.
所以除了极少数几次，我们几乎从没聚在一起过。

762
00:35:30.790 --> 00:35:33.850
And we all really missed John's presence on set,
而且我们都很想念约翰在片场的日子，

763
00:35:33.850 --> 00:35:38.230
so when the branches merged, it was the first time we were all acting together as a group.
所以当分公司合并时，那是我们第一次作为一个整体一起演戏。

764
00:35:38.570 --> 00:35:40.490
And it was a blaSt.
真是太棒了。

765
00:35:40.730 --> 00:35:44.550
Ed Helms made me laugh so loud, I pulled a Phyllis and snorted.
艾德·赫尔姆斯把我逗得大笑，我像菲利斯一样笑出了猪叫声。

766
00:35:45.210 --> 00:35:45.730
Oh!
噢！

767
00:35:47.230 --> 00:35:48.630
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

768
00:35:49.390 --> 00:35:50.810
Yeah, it was great.
是啊，那真的很棒。

769
00:35:51.150 --> 00:35:54.650
It was great to have this new energy and new people,
能有这些新活力和新面孔真是太好了，

770
00:35:54.650 --> 00:35:57.590
and I just have such fun memories of it.
我对那段时光留下了非常有趣的回忆。

771
00:35:57.590 --> 00:36:02.430
Yeah, I will tell you the place where I snort laughed when we get to it.
没错，等讲到那儿的时候，我会告诉你我是在哪儿笑出猪叫的。

772
00:36:02.570 --> 00:36:03.330
Okay, good.
好的，没问题。

773
